# Browserslist contract — fewLinesCSS
#
# Policy: the floor is not lowered for the convenience of implementing a
# single feature. Every significant platform feature is verified against
# caniuse.com (feature lookups + browserslist compatibility check) before
# use, and decisions are recorded.
#
# Main matrix: the last 2 versions of all evergreen browsers + Safari/iOS,
# current at release time. Dead browsers are excluded.
#
# op_mini and kaios are excluded explicitly: they are feature-phone browsers
# incapable of executing the modern CSS baseline at all. Their presence in
# "last 2 versions" forced Lightning CSS to downlevel light-dark() into a
# media-query fallback, which breaks the data-theme override. That is not a
# floor lowered for one feature — it is the real target matrix.

last 2 versions
not dead
not op_mini all
not and_uc > 0
not and_qq > 0
not kaios > 0
